# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c) on a proposal with a yea and a nay (council_p2 after votes_two), and
# the clicks on the leaders' seats, which ask for a vote: the player's own seat (nothing happens), the seat of the faction that is not
# in the game (a notice), a faction at vendetta with the player (a poke gives faction 2 the status bit: it refuses, in a popup), a
# faction that has promised its vote to the player (a poke gives faction 3 the pledge: left be), a click on the window where there is no
# seat, a key that is not Return or Escape (ignored), a seat of an AI that will talk (the popup of yea and nay: Nay chosen, which buys
# the vote, the AI's message), then the player's own Nay button, which decides the vote, a click on a seat after the vote is decided
# (ignored) and Escape, which closes the window (the proposal failed, so it is not carried out). The state regions are as in
# councwin_vote.scene, and the factions' tables (the pledges and the treaty bits are in them).
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
